### Basic Multiple Endpoints for Game Store API

### Get all games
GET https://localhost:7042/games
Accept: application/json

### Get game by ID
GET https://localhost:7042/games/1
Accept: application/json

### Create a new game
POST https://localhost:7042/games
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New Game",
  "genre": "Action",
  "price": 59.99
}

### Update game
PUT https://localhost:7042/games/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Game",
  "price": 49.99
}

### Delete game
DELETE https://localhost:7042/games/1



2. With Comments and Separators

################################
# GAMES ENDPOINTS
################################

### Get All Games
GET https://localhost:7042/games

### Get Single Game
GET https://localhost:7042/games/{{gameId}}

### Create Game
POST https://localhost:7042/games
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sample Game"
}

################################
# USERS ENDPOINTS (if you have)
################################

### Get All Users
GET https://localhost:7042/users

### Create User
POST https://localhost:7042/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}


### 3. Using Variables 

@hostname = localhost
@port = 7042
@host = https://{{hostname}}:{{port}}
@contentType = application/json

### Get all games
GET {{host}}/games
Accept: {{contentType}}

### Get game by ID
GET {{host}}/games/5
Accept: {{contentType}}

### Create game
POST {{host}}/games
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "name": "Cyberpunk 2077",
  "genre": "RPG"
}

### 4. With Request Variables (for dynamic values)

  @baseUrl = https://localhost:7042

### Variable for game ID
@gameId = 1

### Get specific game
GET {{baseUrl}}/games/{{gameId}}

### Or set variable in request
GET {{baseUrl}}/games/{{$guid}}


### 5. Organized by Resource Type


### =========== GAMES ===========
### Get all games
GET https://localhost:7042/games

### Get game by ID
GET https://localhost:7042/games/1

### Create game
POST https://localhost:7042/games
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "title": "New Game"
}

### =========== PLAYERS ===========
### Get all players
GET https://localhost:7042/players

### Create player
POST https://localhost:7042/players
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "name": "Player1"
}

### =========== SCORES ===========
### Get scores for game
GET https://localhost:7042/games/1/scores

### Submit score
POST https://localhost:7042/scores
Content-Type: application/json
{
  "gameId": 1,
  "playerId": 1,
  "score": 1000
}



### 6. With Authentication


@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

### Get games (authenticated)
GET https://localhost:7042/games
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create game (requires auth)
POST https://localhost:7042/games
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Secret Game"
}


Tips for Working with HTTP Files:

    Separate requests with ### on a line by itself

    Click the "Send Request" link above each request in VS Code to execute it


Save responses to variables:

### Login and save token
POST https://localhost:7042/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auth_token", response.body.token);
%}

### Use the token
GET https://localhost:7042/games
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}